From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 14:04:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01018/11362] [outer-loop] GAP-3 Stage 0 adversarially
 confirmed NEGATIVE -> Stage 1 GO

5-reviewer adversarial-verify round (GAP-3 design Section 4) over the Stage-0
q_halt negative: unanimous NEGATIVE_CONFIRMED, worst severity cosmetic, Stage1=GO.
Reviewers independently re-derived every number from the 8041-candidate table (no
torch); none found a de-confounded q ranker that beats vote. Decisive fact:
headroom_capture_fraction=0 -- on the 4 tasks where gold is present but vote misses
top-2, q_mean recovers ZERO (scalar redundant with vote exactly where it must add
value). Positive control holds (oracle 0.613 > vote 0.452). No leak.

- results/arc3_gap3_stage0_adversarial_verify.json: the persisted verdict + reviews.
- Applied the one cosmetic fix: Q_MAX 'best_deconfounded' ties vote with ZERO
  orthogonal lift (hit set byte-identical to vote) -- now annotated honestly.
- ops/verifier_gaps.md GAP-3 build log + design doc Stage-0 marked DONE/NEGATIVE.

Next: Stage 1 (TRM penultimate-activation latent) -- needs a GPU activation-dump
re-run (conductor/timer pause). The 0.86 within-task soft-AUROC is the leading
indicator the full latent carries sharper vote-orthogonal signal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
